  "scope": "The actual 48-slot positive-cost inventory traverses the original aligned vertex-word and rational-row lists. It saves their literal cursors, calls the real numerator-bit zero test, skips zero costs and allocates retained records containing the original rational and index-word pointers. Ordered recursion returns exactly the original positiveIndices values, including padding and duplicate word occurrences. The returned inventory derives the existing stable argmin input representation without an externally supplied positive list. The same physical run preserves original inputs, source and stack, with exact allocated cells and a terminal-inclusive bound in original bit/list sizes. Twelve physical cases check empty/all-zero/mixed/all-positive/padded and duplicate-pointer behavior. The actual argmin call, exact minimumPositive output, original-width construction, guess preparation and complete solver join remain separate.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
}
